   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is inevitable",
     "texto": [
      "To say that there is no other option, that something is inevitable, use **-(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다**: 가다 → **갈 수밖에 없어요** (there is no choice but to go), 기다리다 → **기다릴 수밖에 없어요** (there is nothing to do but wait), 먹다 → **먹을 수밖에 없어요** (there is nothing but to eat).",
      "버스가 없어서 걸어**갈 수밖에 없어요** = as there is no bus, there is nothing to do but walk there."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tone",
     "texto": [
      "It expresses that, given the circumstances, there is no other viable alternative. It can sound like resignation, but it does not require the option to be unpleasant. It is distinguished from **-지 않으면 안 되다**, which presents an obligation.",
      "버스가 없어서 걸어갈 **수밖에 없어요** = as there is no bus, there is no other option but to walk there."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
